xnu 0469: map the boot windows before any worker that maps

Measured 2026-11-26: with 0468 in, the wifi worker stopped at
`W4 BAR map done` instead of reaching the firmware load. `mondrian_wifi_start()`
is called inside `mondrian_usb_probe()`, so the worker runs while the boot
probe block still maps the restart-reason IMEM and the SPMI SDAM window; a
second `ml_io_map()` racing a worker that maps wedges both (the same trap that
stalls a late 1 MiB BAR map).

The two mappings now happen before `mondrian_gpu_probe()` and the USB probe, so
every boot-time window is in place before any thread starts.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index ae96660..bb4cfcb 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2402,6 +2402,15 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		extern void mondrian_spmi_probe(void);
 		extern void mondrian_reset_reason_init(void);
 
+		/*
+		 * Both map MMIO and must run before any worker that maps: the
+		 * wifi thread starts inside mondrian_usb_probe(), and a second
+		 * ml_io_map() racing it wedges both (measured 2026-11-26, the
+		 * worker stopped at `W4 BAR map done`). The key thread the SPMI
+		 * probe starts only reads windows these calls mapped.
+		 */
+		mondrian_reset_reason_init();
+		mondrian_spmi_probe();
 		(void)mondrian_gpu_probe();
 		mondrian_touch_probe();
 		mondrian_usb_probe();
@@ -2409,8 +2418,6 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		mondrian_venus_start();
 		mondrian_bt_tty_init();
 		mondrian_bt_ctl_init();
-		mondrian_reset_reason_init();
-		mondrian_spmi_probe();
 	}
 }
 
